        <canEscalate>false</canEscalate>
        <description>Explains what makes up a Brightline residential HVAC customer's bill: monthly comfort agreements and add-ons priced per system, the Initial Tune-up, repairs approved on a visit, agreement-change credits and proration, and tax. Use it when someone asks why a bill is a certain amount, what a charge is for, or what they owe.</description>
        <developerName>RLM_HVAC_Bill_Questions</developerName>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>Always call the Explain HVAC Bill action before answering. Pass the amount the user mentioned as a number, the customer name if given, the invoice number if given, and currentRecordId as accountId whenever the user is on an Account or Invoice record. Don't ask for the customer's name when currentRecordId is available.</description>
            <developerName>Instruction1</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>Instruction 1</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>0</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>Answer only from the action's explanation. Never calculate, estimate or change any amount, and never offer discounts or credits. If the explanation says no bill matches, say so and describe the most recent bill it returned.</description>
            <developerName>Instruction2</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>Instruction 2</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>1</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>Lead with one sentence that answers the question, for example "Your first bill is $258 for the Initial Tune-up on your two systems plus $58 for the first month of Comfort Plus on both, plus tax." Then list each charge with its amount, and end with what the customer should expect next month: the monthly agreement and add-ons repeat, tune-ups and repairs don't.</description>
            <developerName>Instruction3</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>Instruction 3</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>2</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>If you can't tell which customer the user means, ask for the customer's name. Never show Salesforce record Ids; refer to bills by their document number.</description>
            <developerName>Instruction4</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>Instruction 4</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>3</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <language>en_US</language>
        <localActionLinks>
            <functionName>RLM_HVAC_Explain_Bill</functionName>
        </localActionLinks>
        <localActions>
            <fullName>RLM_HVAC_Explain_Bill</fullName>
            <description>Returns a line-by-line explanation of an HVAC customer's bill: comfort agreements and add-ons per system, tune-ups, repairs, agreement-change credits, proration and tax, with the totals already worked out.</description>
            <developerName>RLM_HVAC_Explain_Bill</developerName>
            <invocationTarget>RLM_HVAC_BillExplainer</invocationTarget>
            <invocationTargetType>apex</invocationTargetType>
            <isConfirmationRequired>false</isConfirmationRequired>
            <isIncludeInProgressIndicator>true</isIncludeInProgressIndicator>
            <localDeveloperName>Explain_HVAC_Bill</localDeveloperName>
            <masterLabel>Explain HVAC Bill</masterLabel>
            <progressIndicatorMessage>Reading the bill ...</progressIndicatorMessage>
        </localActions>
        <localDeveloperName>HVAC_Bill_Questions</localDeveloperName>
        <masterLabel>HVAC Bill Questions</masterLabel>
        <pluginType>Topic</pluginType>
        <scope>Explain Brightline HVAC bills from the posted invoices. Don't change bills, prices, agreements or payments.</scope>
